    "appliesToWoo": true,
    "appliesToWooNote": "wc/v3 inherits the same base collection params, so the 100 cap applies to wc/v3 too. 🚩 The Woo DOCS do NOT state a cap — the SOURCE is the authority here.",
    "driftRisk": "OFFSET-based, therefore DRIFT-PRONE under concurrent writes on deep pages: rows shift across page boundaries and a deep full scan can skip or duplicate records. Deep paging is also O(offset) in the database and that, not a documented cap on `page`, is the practical wall.",
    "driftMitigation": "A STABLE SORT (orderby=id&order=asc). This reduces but does not eliminate the drift. The connector declares best-effort completeness for a deep full scan — it does NOT claim exactness. See DeclaredCapabilityLimits.offset-pagination-drift.",
    "evidence": "packages/Integration/connectors-registry/wordpress/sources/wp-7.1/wp-includes/rest-api/endpoints/class-wp-rest-controller.php:352-357 ; https://developer.wordpress.org/rest-api/using-the-rest-api/pagination/"
  },
  "IncrementalSyncCapability": {
    "supported": "partial",
    "note": "🚩 UNEVEN, AND THE UNEVENNESS IS PER-CONTROLLER-BASE-CLASS, NOT PER-NAMESPACE. Whether a family supports a watermark is decided by which base class its controller extends, so it cannot be inferred from the namespace or from the docs. Two families that a naive reading treats as incremental are NOT: wp/v2/users and wc/v3/customers.",
    "fullWatermark": {
