      "note": "This is the PRECISE capability, proven from source, and it is identical for both families. UPDATES REMAIN INVISIBLE. It must NOT be rounded up to \"incremental supported\", and NO IncrementalWatermarkField may be emitted. On wp/v2/users the ordering itself requires the `list_users` capability. See DeclaredCapabilityLimits.users-no-incremental and .woo-customers-no-incremental."
    },
    "none": {
      "families": "wc/v3/orders/<id>/notes ; and the config/reference resources — product attributes + attribute terms, product categories, product tags, product brands, product shipping classes, taxes, tax classes, shipping zones / zone locations / zone methods, shipping methods, payment gateways, settings groups, setting options, system status, system status tools, data (countries/currencies/continents), customer downloads.",
      "note": "No date filters and no modified fields. Full-scan only — acceptable, since these are small slow-changing reference sets."
    },
    "deletes": "NONE. See DeclaredCapabilityLimits.no-deleted-records-feed — there is no deleted-records feed anywhere, and deletion reconciliation is a declared KEY SWEEP, not detection.",
    "inferenceRule": "NEVER infer support from a 200 response — an unrecognised arg is SILENTLY IGNORED rather than rejected. Read the arg list from OPTIONS <route>."
  },
  "WebhooksAvailable": true,
  "WebhooksNote": "WooCommerce ONLY. wc/v3 registers a first-class webhooks resource — /wc/v3/webhooks, /wc/v3/webhooks/{id}, /wc/v3/webhooks/batch — present in the derived in-scope spec, with after/before (created date) collection params. WordPress CORE has NO webhook API at all: nothing in wp/v2 registers or delivers hooks. So webhook availability is conditional on WooCommerce being installed AND on the connection carrying a credential able to reach wc/v3.",
  "WebhooksSignatureAlgorithm": null,
  "WebhooksSignatureHeader": null,
  "WebhooksSignatureGap": "🚩 GAP, deliberately left NULL rather than guessed. The webhook delivery/signing code (includes/class-wc-webhook.php) is NOT in the acquired pinned file set — the local Woo 11.0.1 extraction covers includes/rest-api, includes/admin and includes/wccom-site only. The signature algorithm and header name are therefore NOT PROVABLE from the pinned sources on this run, and no value is recorded. A later phase with the full plugin tree, or a live OPTIONS/delivery observation, must fill this in.",
  "BulkOperationsAvailable": true,
  "BulkOperationsNote": "🚩 BATCHING IS WRITE-ONLY. READS ARE NOT BATCHABLE ANYWHERE. Stating this honestly because the naive read of \"the API supports batch\" is that a bulk read exists — it does not, in core or in Woo v3.",
  "BatchCapability": {
    "core": {
      "basePath": "/batch/v1",
